    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full test suite (including the new `coreNumericLevel` acceptance test) is green, and the audit log now emits `membershipLevel=3`.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced `getMembershipTier()` (String, GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) with `getMembershipLevel()` (int): starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (documenting that level 4 is reserved for tenure). Still derived from stored state, never persisted \u2014 consistent with the prior pattern.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the `membershipTier` (string) response property and added `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1 / max 3, `readOnly`). MapStruct auto-maps it from the new getter by name, so `OwnerMapper` needed no change.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel` instead of the (formerly absent) tier, per the spec's requirement that anything recording the tier record the level.\n- **`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 removed the now-stale javadoc reference to `getMembershipTier()`/GOLD, since household size no longer contributes to the level.\n\nEach concern stayed in its own small unit: the level rule lives on the entity, the schema in OpenAPI, and the audit in its function class.\n\nNote: `householdSize` is still computed and persisted at creation (used elsewhere); only its link to membership was removed, since the new level rule intentionally drops the household/GOLD component.",
